      "read-only (InvArgs). With Specific, vma_offset counts from the region's",
      "start and must be page-aligned (InvArgs); the region must have",
      "CanMapSpecific (AccessDenied, asked before whether the range lies",
      "inside it; a process's root region has it), the range must lie inside",
      "it (InvArgs) and overlap nothing already there (AlreadyExists).",
      "Without Specific, vma_offset must be 0 (InvArgs) and the kernel finds",
      "room (NotFound when there is none). BadState once the region's address",
      "space has been torn down. If |mapped_addr| cannot be written",
      "(InvArgs), the mapping is taken down again, except a Sealed one, which",
      "stays.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vma"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "VmOptions"
      },
      {
        name = "vma_offset"
        type = "usize"
      },
      {
        name = "vmo"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "vmo_offset"
        type = "u64"
      },
      {
        name = "length"
        type = "usize"
      },
      {
        name = "mapped_addr"
        type = "VirtAddr"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "vma_unmap"
    brief = "Unmaps whatever lies in part of the region |vma|."
    doc = [
      "Tears down everything in [addr, addr + length) of |vma|, length rounded",
      "up to a page. A mapping wholly inside the range goes; one partly inside",
      "loses the pages inside it but keeps its range, which nothing else can",
      "take until the whole mapping is unmapped. A sub-region wholly inside the",
      "range is destroyed with everything in it, and its handles answer",
      "BadState from then on; that needs OpChildren on |vma| (InvArgs without",
      "it). A range that only partly covers a sub-region is InvArgs. A range",
      "that overlaps a Sealed mapping, here or in any sub-region below, the",
      "vDSO's code among them, is AccessDenied. Any refusal unmaps nothing. An",
      "|addr| that is not page-aligned, a |length| of 0 or one too large to",
      "round up, and a range not wholly inside |vma| are InvArgs. A range with",
      "nothing in it is Ok. No right is needed on |vma|.",
      "BadState once the region has been destroyed, with its address space or",
      "by an unmap of its parent.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vma"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "addr"
        type = "VirtAddr"
      },
      {
        name = "length"
        type = "usize"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "vmo_create_child"
    brief =
        "Creates a slice or a copy-on-write snapshot of the VMO |vmo| names."
    doc = [
      "|options| is one of Slice, SnapshotFull, SnapshotOnWrite and",
      "SnapshotModified, alone; any other combination of named bits, None",
      "included, is NotSupported, an unknown bit InvArgs. A slice is the",
      "window [offset, offset + size) of the parent, over the same pages, so",
      "a write through either is seen through the other; |offset| must be",
      "page-aligned and the range must lie inside the parent (InvArgs). A",
      "snapshot is a copy-on-write copy of that range: neither side sees the",
      "other's later writes (all three kinds are built as SnapshotFull). Its",
      "|offset| must be page-aligned and no further than the parent's end",
      "(InvArgs); the range may run past the end, and reads as zero there.",
      "BadState for a snapshot of a VMO whose pages are pinned, such as the",
      "vDSO's. |size| rounds up to a page; OutOfRange past the largest size a",
      "VMO can have. NotSupported on a VMO that is a window onto physical",
      "memory. The handle must grant Duplicate and Read (AccessDenied). A",
      "slice's handle has the same rights; a snapshot's has them with Write",
      "added and Execute taken away. Its value goes to |out|, and it is in",
      "this process's table only once that write has worked: InvArgs, and no",
      "new handle, when |out| cannot be written. It counts against this",
      "process's handle quota: NoResource past it, or when the handle arena",
      "is full.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vmo"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "VmoChildOptions"
      },
      {
        name = "offset"
        type = "u64"
      },
      {
        name = "size"
        type = "u64"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "vmo_replace_as_executable"
    brief = "Replaces |vmo| with a handle to the same VMO that may be executed."
    doc = [
      "|vmex| must name a System resource covering the VMEX slot",
      "(AccessDenied for Uandle::Invalid, BadHandle for a value naming",
      "nothing, BadType for anything but a System resource, OutOfRange for",
      "one of another slot); no right is required of it. |vmo| is consumed",
      "whatever the answer -- duplicate it first to keep a copy -- and",
      "BadHandle when it names nothing or is not a VMO. The new handle has",
      "|vmo|'s rights less Write, plus Execute. Its value goes to |out|, and",
      "it is in this process's table only once that write has worked. It",
      "counts against this process's handle quota: NoResource past it, or",
      "when the handle arena is full.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vmo"
        type = "Uandle"
        release = true
      },
      {
        name = "vmex"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "vmo_write"
    brief =
        "Copies |length| bytes from |buffer| into the VMO, from byte |offset|."
    doc = [
      "Needs Write on |vmo|. OutOfRange when the range does not lie wholly",
      "inside the VMO, and nothing is written then. InvArgs when |buffer|",
      "cannot give |length| bytes -- outside the user half, or not readable",
      "all the way; the VMO may have been written in part before the kernel",
      "found out, so after a failure the range's contents are unspecified.",
      "Writing 0 bytes checks the handle and the offset and touches nothing.",
      "NotSupported on a VMO that is a window onto physical memory rather",
      "than pages of its own.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vmo"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "buffer"
        type = "void"
        dir = "in"
        count = "length"
      },
      {
        name = "offset"
        type = "u64"
      },
      {
        name = "length"
        type = "usize"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "vmo_get_size"
    brief = "Writes the size of the VMO |vmo| names, in bytes, to |size|."
    doc = [
      "No right is needed of |vmo|: whoever holds a handle to a VMO may ask",
      "how big it is. BadHandle when |vmo| names nothing,",
      "BadType when it names something that is not a VMO. The size is the",
      "bound vmo_read, vmo_write and vma_map check a range against, and a",
      "whole number of pages: vmo_create and vmo_create_child round the size",
      "they are given up to a page, so a slice of a 5-byte file is a page",
      "long, and its tail is whatever its parent holds there. A slice's size",
      "is its window's, not its parent's. It never changes, since no VMO is",
      "resizable yet. InvArgs when |size| cannot be written.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "vmo"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "size"
        type = "u64"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "handle_duplicate"
    brief = "Makes a second handle to the object |handle| names, with |rights|."
    doc = [
      "|handle| needs Duplicate (AccessDenied). |rights| is SameRights for",
      "the same rights as |handle|, or any subset of them -- none included,",
      "more never (InvArgs); SameRights means that only as the whole word.",
      "The new handle's value goes to |out|, and it is in this process's",
      "table only once that write has worked: InvArgs, and no new handle,",
      "when |out| cannot be written. It counts against this process's handle",
      "quota: NoResource past it, or when the handle arena is full. |handle|",
      "is left as it was, whatever the answer.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "rights"
        type = "Rights"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "task_create_exception_channel"
    brief = "Binds a new exception channel to the task |handle| names, and writes its reading end to |out|."
    doc = [
      "From then on, every exception a thread of the task raises is sent on",
      "the channel as one message: an ExceptionInfo (<ours/exception.hpp>)",
      "and one handle, the exception's. The thread waits until that handle",
      "is closed; Property::ExceptionState, set on it first with",
      "object_set_property, says what happens then. The end written to |out|",
      "can be read and waited on and nothing else (Transfer, Wait, Read).",
      "A thread's channel is told before its process's, and hands out no",
      "process (exception_get_process answers AccessDenied). A job answers",
      "NotSupported, any other object BadType. |handle| needs Inspect,",
      "Duplicate, Transfer and ManageThread, and Enumerate for a process",
      "(AccessDenied). One channel per task: AlreadyBound while one is bound",
      "and its reader is still there, BadState once the task is dead.",
      "|options| must be None (InvArgs). The value goes to |out| before the",
      "channel is bound: InvArgs, and nothing bound, when |out| cannot be",
      "written.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "ExceptionChannelOptions"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "object_set_property"
    brief = "Sets |property| of the object |handle| names to the |size| bytes at |value|."
    doc = [
      "Each property has its own value layout and the objects that have it",
      "(<ours/object_property.hpp>). ExceptionState is the only one: on an",
      "exception handle, an ExceptionState, TryNext or Handled (InvArgs",
      "otherwise), to take effect when the handle is closed. |handle| needs",
      "SetProperty (AccessDenied) and must name an object with |property|",
      "(BadType). A |size| below the value's is BufferTooSmall, a |value|",
      "the kernel cannot read InvArgs, an unknown |property| InvArgs.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "property"
        type = "Property"
      },
      {
        name = "value"
        type = "void"
        dir = "in"
        count = "size"
      },
      {
        name = "size"
        type = "usize"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "exception_get_thread"
    brief = "Writes to |out| a new handle to the thread that raised the exception |handle| names."
    doc = [
      "The handle's rights are those of the task handle the exception's",
      "channel was bound with (task_create_exception_channel), so a handler",
      "gets no more than whoever bound the channel had. |handle| needs no",
      "right, and must name an exception (BadType). The new handle counts",
      "against this process's handle quota: NoResource past it, or when the",
      "arena is full. The value goes to |out| before the handle is",
      "installed: InvArgs, and no handle, when |out| cannot be written.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "exception_get_process"
    brief = "Writes to |out| a new handle to the process of the thread that raised the exception |handle| names."
    doc = [
      "As exception_get_thread, for the faulting thread's process. A",
      "channel bound to a thread hands out no process (AccessDenied): it",
      "grants no way up the task chain.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "interrupt_create"
    brief = "Makes an interrupt object and writes a handle to it into |out|."
    doc = [
      "An interrupt object is something a thread waits on for an interrupt",
      "to arrive (interrupt_wait). |options| must be Virtual: an interrupt",
      "with no line behind it, raised only by interrupt_trigger. A virtual",
      "interrupt needs no resource, so |resource| and |line| are not looked",
      "at. Options without Virtual name a physical line, which is",
      "NotSupported until physical lines arrive; an option this kernel does",
      "not know is InvArgs. The handle has Transfer, Duplicate, Wait,",
      "Inspect, Read, Write and Signal.",
      "Closing its last handle destroys the object.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "resource"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "line"
        type = "u32"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "InterruptOptions"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "interrupt_wait"
    brief = "Waits for the next interrupt on |handle| and writes when it arrived to |out_timestamp|."
    doc = [
      "Returns at once if one is pending. Taking one is also the ack of the",
      "one taken before it, which is why later interrupts only fold into the",
      "pending one until a wait takes it: the time written is the first's.",
      "Cancelled when the object is destroyed, before the wait or during",
      "it. BadState while another thread is waiting on the same object.",
      "|handle| must name an interrupt (BadType) with Wait (AccessDenied).",
      "|out_timestamp| may be null; one that cannot be written answers",
      "InvArgs, with the interrupt taken.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "out_timestamp"
        type = "Instant"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = [ "blocking" ]
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "interrupt_trigger"
    brief = "Raises the virtual interrupt |handle| names, as having arrived at |timestamp|."
    doc = [
      "A thread waiting on it wakes, or the next wait returns at once. If",
      "an interrupt is already pending, it keeps its own time. Only a",
      "virtual interrupt can be raised (BadState), and not once destroyed",
      "(Cancelled). |options| must be None (InvArgs). |handle| must name an",
      "interrupt (BadType) with Signal (AccessDenied).",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "InterruptTriggerOptions"
      },
      {
        name = "timestamp"
        type = "Instant"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "interrupt_destroy"
    brief = "Destroys the interrupt object |handle| names."
    doc = [
      "Its line, if it has one, is let go of, and a thread waiting on it",
      "wakes with Cancelled, as does every later wait or trigger. The handle",
      "stays open; destroying again is Ok. |handle| must name an interrupt",
      "(BadType); no right is needed.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "sampler_create"
    brief = "Makes a sampling profiler session and writes a handle to it into |out|."
    doc = [
      "A session samples every online CPU every |config|'s period once",
      "started, recording into per-CPU buffers of |config|'s buffer size;",
      "see SamplerConfig. There is one session at a time: AlreadyExists while",
      "another exists, until its last handle is closed. |resource| must name",
      "a System resource covering the SAMPLING slot (BadHandle, BadType,",
      "OutOfRange). |options| must be 0, |config|'s reserved field 0, its",
      "targets at least one known target, its period from",
      "SAMPLER_MIN_PERIOD to SAMPLER_MAX_PERIOD and its buffer size from one",
      "record to SAMPLER_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE (InvArgs). The user target is",
      "NotSupported yet. The handle has Transfer, Duplicate and Inspect; no",
      "call on it asks for a right. Closing its last handle stops the",
      "session and ends it.",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "resource"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "options"
        type = "u64"
      },
      {
        name = "config"
        type = "SamplerConfig"
        dir = "in"
      },
      {
        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "sampler_start"
    brief = "Starts the session |handle| names sampling."
    doc = [
      "Empties its buffers and arms every online CPU's sampling timer before",
      "it returns. BadState while the session runs, or while a",
      "sampler_read on it is copying. |handle| must name a sampler",
      "(BadType).",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "sampler_stop"
    brief = "Stops the session |handle| names."
    doc = [
      "When it returns no CPU is recording into the session any more, and",
      "its samples can be read. BadState unless the session runs. |handle|",
      "must name a sampler (BadType).",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "sampler_read"
    brief = "Copies the stopped session's samples into |data| and writes how many bytes into |actual|."
    doc = [
      "The bytes are a SamplerDumpHeader, then every CPU's retained",
      "SamplerRecords in CPU order (<ours/sampler.hpp>). With |data| null,",
      "|actual| gets the size they need; with",
      "|data_size| less than that, BufferTooSmall, and |actual| gets the",
      "size. A copy that faults stops there and answers the fault's status,",
      "with |actual| at the bytes copied before it. BadState while the",
      "session runs. |handle| must name a sampler (BadType).",
    ]
    args = [
      {
        name = "handle"
        type = "Uandle"
      },
      {
        name = "data"
        type = "void"
        dir = "out"
        count = "data_size"
      },
      {
        name = "data_size"
        type = "usize"
      },
      {
        name = "actual"
        type = "usize"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
]
